# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
COMBOS_DEEP = [
 dict(id="SE-027", ways=5, name="The Signal Box",
  parents="RCS 001 (Cascading Recalculation) + RCS 013 (Monte Carlo) + Dr. Buddy 09 (Crisis Detection) + JoinAQAL PAT-004 (Weakness) + Drass DR-02 (Compliance Gate)",
  metaphor="a railway signal box where no train moves until every point on its route is set",
  simple="In an old signal box the levers are locked against each other, so a signal cannot clear while the points ahead are wrong. The mechanism makes the unsafe move physically impossible. This invention does that for a financial plan: nothing recalculates and nothing displays until every dependency and every guard agrees. A plan cannot arrive at the screen in a half-changed state. The interlock is in the machine, not the procedure.",
  works="When one figure changes, the system works out everything downstream of it and the order those must move in. Thousands of scenarios are re-run against the new state, and the crisis and weakness signals are checked as part of the same pass. Only when all of it settles, and the compliance gate agrees, does anything appear. A failure anywhere leaves the previous good state on screen rather than a partial new one.",
  patentable="Financial tools recalculate optimistically and repair inconsistencies afterward, if at all. The emergent capability is a plan that is never observable in an inconsistent state, achieved by interlocking recalculation, simulation, risk detection and compliance into a single atomic step.",
  alice=8, alice_why="Atomic multi-engine state transition is squarely technical; this is one of the strongest eligibility positions in the portfolio.",
  priority="Critical to file",
  urgency="Atomicity across heterogeneous engines is genuinely hard and genuinely valuable, which is the combination that makes a patent worth owning. It also describes an architecture a competitor cannot easily design around, because the alternative is the inconsistency you are avoiding. Five parents make the claim dense and hard to invalidate piecemeal. This belongs in the very first filing batch."),
 dict(id="SE-028", ways=5, name="The Grafted Orchard",
  parents="JoinAQAL PAT-001 (Consensus) + JoinAQAL PAT-005 (Coaching) + Dr. Buddy 07 (Multi-Agent Clinical) + Dr. Buddy 02 (Digital Twin) + RCS 011 (Advisor Scoring)",
  metaphor="grafting branches from several trees onto one rootstock so the fruit is unlike any parent",
  simple="Graft branches from different trees onto one trunk and you get fruit none of the parent trees could produce. This invention grafts several panels of AI together on a single root: one panel scores the person, one plans their care, one plans their money, and one scores the humans advising them. The fruit is a recommendation that carries the judgement of all of them. No single panel could have grown it.",
  works="Each panel works independently and produces its own answer with its own confidence. A digital copy of the person is used to test the combined recommendation before any human sees it. Advisors are scored on how their past recommendations actually turned out, and that score weights how much their input counts next time. The system learns which voices to trust from outcomes rather than from seniority.",
  patentable="Multi-agent systems normally weight members by design or by static configuration. Weighting human advisors by measured outcome inside the same loop that weights AI panels is new. The emergent capability is a recommendation engine whose trust in each contributor, human or machine, is earned from results.",
  alice=7, alice_why="Outcome-weighted contributor scoring is the concrete inventive step; the multi-agent framing alone would not carry it.",
  priority="High importance",
  urgency="The advisor scoring element is commercially explosive because it changes how a firm pays people. That also means it will be contested, so an early priority date matters more than usual. Four of the five parents are already built, leaving one clear gap to close before filing. Target the second batch and close that gap first."),
 dict(id="SE-029", ways=6, name="The Reservoir And The Dam",
  parents="RCS 009 (Mortgage Elimination) + RCS 002 (HELOC-to-IUL) + RCS 012 (Roth with STR) + RCS 005 (Income Waterfall) + JoinAQAL PAT-004 (Weakness) + Dr. Buddy 08 (Automated Report)",
  metaphor="a reservoir system where every gate opening is timed against every other",
  simple="A reservoir is not one wall. It is a series of gates, and opening them in the wrong order floods the valley. This invention sequences a family's money moves the same way: the house, the borrowing, the conversions and the withdrawals all have a right order and a right moment. Open them together and the tax bill drowns you. Opened in sequence, the same water arrives safely downstream. The plan is written out afterward in plain language.",
  works="Four financial mechanisms that each work alone are placed on a single timeline, with each one's opening conditioned on the state the others have reached. The person's own biggest weakness is used to decide which gates they can realistically operate and which should be automated. When the sequence is settled, a readable report explains what happens, in what order, and why.",
  patentable="Each mechanism is separately known; nobody has interlocked all four on a dependency timeline gated by the individual's measured behavioural weakness. The emergent capability is a multi-year sequence that accounts for whether this particular person will actually execute each step.",
  alice=7, alice_why="The dependency-gated sequencing is technical; the underlying financial strategies are not, so claim the scheduler.",
  priority="High importance",
  urgency="This is the richest single offer in the catalogue and the one most likely to be reverse-engineered from a client illustration. The behavioural gating is the part nobody else has and the part that makes the sequence actually work in practice. Six parents give it real defensive depth against piecemeal challenge. File once the sequencing engine is demonstrable end to end."),
 dict(id="SE-030", ways=8, name="The Telescope Array",
  parents="All 7 JoinAQAL patents + Dr. Buddy 13 (Integrated Platform)",
  metaphor="a field of small telescopes linked to act as one enormous mirror",
  simple="Astronomers link many modest telescopes so they behave as one giant mirror, seeing detail no single dish could resolve. This invention links every measuring instrument in the cognitive platform and points them at one person through the clinical platform's frame. Each instrument is ordinary alone. Combined and aimed together, they resolve detail about a person that none of them could see separately.",
  works="All seven assessment engines run on the same person and their outputs are aligned to a shared frame of reference rather than simply listed. The clinical platform supplies that frame, so cognitive findings are expressed in terms a care plan can act on. Where instruments disagree, the disagreement is preserved and pointed at, because that is usually where something interesting is. Everything is written to a record that can only be appended.",
  patentable="Assessment suites report their subtests separately and leave synthesis to a human. Aligning all seven to a clinical frame, and treating instrument disagreement as a first-class finding, is new. The emergent capability is a resolution of detail about a person that is genuinely unavailable from any subset of the instruments.",
  alice=8, alice_why="Frame-aligned multi-instrument synthesis with preserved disagreement is a concrete data-processing improvement.",
  priority="Critical to file",
  urgency="This is the umbrella over the entire JoinAQAL portfolio, and umbrella claims are what survive when individual claims get narrowed. It is also the clearest expression of why the seven patents are worth more together than apart, which matters for valuation as much as for protection. All seven parents are built and running. File it as the anchor of the JoinAQAL family."),
 dict(id="SE-031", ways=10, name="The Watchmaker's Escapement",
  parents="RCS 001, 003, 005, 008, 013 + Dr. Buddy 09, 10, 11 + JoinAQAL PAT-004, PAT-007",
  metaphor="an escapement that lets a mainspring release its energy one measured tick at a time",
  simple="A wound mainspring wants to release all its force instantly. The escapement is the small clever part that lets it out one tick at a time, which is the only reason a watch tells time instead of exploding. This invention is the escapement for a person's whole financial and emotional picture: enormous pressure, released in measured steps the person can actually absorb. Ten mechanisms, one regulated tick.",
  works="The financial engines know what should happen. The clinical engines know how much the person can take right now. The transparency layer decides how much can be explained honestly at each step. Instead of delivering the full plan at once, the system releases it in increments timed to the person's measured capacity, and re-measures after each one. Pressure that would overwhelm is held back rather than discarded.",
  patentable="Financial planning delivers the whole plan and hopes the client copes; clinical pacing tools do not touch money. Pacing the release of financial change against continuously measured psychological capacity is unprecedented. The emergent capability is a plan that gets executed rather than abandoned, because it arrives at a survivable rate.",
  alice=8, alice_why="Capacity-gated incremental release with feedback re-measurement is a specific control mechanism, not an abstract idea.",
  priority="Critical to file",
  urgency="Abandonment is the real enemy of every financial plan, and this addresses it at the mechanism level rather than with encouragement. Ten parents make it extremely hard to design around, since a competitor needs most of the stack to reproduce it. It is also the most defensible expression of why the three platforms belong in one company. Put it in the first batch alongside the signal box."),
 dict(id="SE-032", ways=12, name="The Mycelium Under The Forest",
  parents="RCS 001, 004, 007, 008, 011 + Dr. Buddy 01, 02, 09, 13 + JoinAQAL PAT-001, PAT-006 + Drass DR-01",
  metaphor="the fungal network under a forest, moving nutrients between trees that never touch",
  simple="Under a forest runs a fungal network that quietly moves nutrients from a thriving tree to a struggling one, though the trees never touch. This invention is that network for a household. What is learned in one part of a family's life feeds the parts that need it, across platforms that never directly connect. The person sees healthy trees. They never see the network doing the work.",
  works="Findings from any platform are expressed in a shared internal language rather than passed as raw records. That shared form lets a clinical finding inform a financial risk model, or a cognitive finding reshape a care plan, without either platform needing to understand the other's internals. The licensed delivery shell exposes the results without ever holding the network itself. Nothing crosses that could identify a person outside the boundary it belongs in.",
  patentable="Cross-domain data sharing is normally record-level integration, which is exactly what privacy rules obstruct. Sharing at the level of derived findings in a shared abstract form, with identifying detail never crossing, is new. The emergent capability is genuine cross-domain intelligence that remains compartmentalised.",
  alice=8, alice_why="An abstraction layer that carries derived findings while provably excluding identifiers is a technical privacy architecture.",
  priority="Critical to file",
  urgency="This is the answer to the privacy objection that will otherwise block every multi-platform ambition you have. Filing it converts your biggest regulatory liability into an owned asset. Twelve parents make the claim formidable, and the shared-abstraction step is the kind of idea a determined competitor arrives at independently within a year or two. It is arguably the single most strategically important filing in this document."),
 dict(id="SE-033", ways=15, name="The Cathedral Scaffold",
  parents="RCS 001, 002, 003, 005, 007, 008, 009, 011, 013 + Dr. Buddy 01, 09, 13 + JoinAQAL PAT-001, PAT-004 + Drass DR-02",
  metaphor="scaffolding that is built, moved and dismantled around a cathedral as the stone rises",
  simple="A cathedral takes generations, and the scaffolding is rebuilt many times as the walls climb. The scaffold is never the point, but nothing rises without it. This invention is the scaffolding around a family's wealth across decades: it assembles where work is happening, holds while the structure sets, and comes down when it is no longer needed. Fifteen mechanisms, appearing and retiring as the building demands. The family sees the cathedral, not the poles.",
  works="The system decides which mechanisms are relevant to this household at this stage of life and activates only those. As circumstances change, mechanisms retire and others stand up, with the compliance gate governing what may be shown at each stage. Crisis detection can freeze the whole structure if the family is in no state to build. Nothing runs simply because it exists.",
  patentable="Comprehensive platforms expose everything and let the user choose; this one decides what should exist for this household right now and withholds the rest. The emergent capability is that complexity scales with the family's actual situation rather than with the vendor's feature list.",
  alice=7, alice_why="Lifecycle-driven activation and retirement of engines is technical; guard against reading as menu configuration.",
  priority="High importance",
  urgency="This is how the platform stays usable as it grows, which is the failure mode that kills comprehensive software. Fifteen parents make it a strong umbrella over most of the RCS portfolio at once. Its value rises as you add tools, so filing now protects work not yet built. Second batch, after the atomic and privacy claims are secured."),
 dict(id="SE-034", ways=20, name="The Tide That Moves The Whole Harbour",
  parents="All 4 platforms, 20 engines: RCS 001, 003, 004, 005, 007, 008, 011, 013 + Dr. Buddy 01, 02, 09, 10, 11, 13 + JoinAQAL PAT-001, PAT-004, PAT-005, PAT-007 + Drass DR-02, DR-03",
  metaphor="a tide that lifts every boat in a harbour at once, whatever size and wherever moored",
  simple="A tide does not visit each boat in turn. It raises the whole harbour at once, the dinghy and the trawler alike, and every mooring line adjusts itself. This invention moves a person's entire picture in one motion: what they know about themselves, how they are coping, what their money is doing, and who is helping them. One change, everything rises together. Nothing is left at the old level waiting to be updated.",
  works="A single verified change anywhere is expressed in the shared internal language and propagated to every engine that depends on it, in dependency order, as one transaction. Twenty mechanisms across four platforms settle into a consistent new state or none of them move at all. Compliance and crisis guards can veto the whole motion. The person experiences one coherent update rather than four systems disagreeing for an afternoon.",
  patentable="No system propagates a single change across cognitive, clinical, financial and delivery domains as one atomic transaction with domain-specific veto rights. The emergent capability is that four independent businesses behave as one organism without merging their data, their databases or their companies.",
  alice=7, alice_why="Distributed atomic commit with domain vetoes is strongly technical; breadth is the risk, so dependent claims must stake narrower ground.",
  priority="High importance",
  urgency="This is the capstone claim that describes the whole enterprise in one invention, and capstones are valuable precisely because they are hard to work around. Its breadth is also its weakness, so it must be filed with narrower dependent claims beneath it rather than alone. It should follow the atomic and privacy filings, which give it firm ground to stand on. Treat it as the roof, not the foundation."),
 dict(id="SE-035", ways=20, name="The Seed Vault",
  parents="All 4 platforms, 20 engines spanning every family: RCS 001, 002, 005, 008, 009, 010, 013 + Dr. Buddy 01, 02, 05, 09, 12, 13, 14 + JoinAQAL PAT-001, PAT-003, PAT-004 + Drass DR-01, DR-02, DR-04",
  metaphor="an arctic seed vault holding varieties nobody is planting yet",
  simple="Deep in the arctic sits a vault of seeds for crops nobody is growing right now, kept because someday someone will need them. This invention is that vault for a person's own history. Every measurement, every plan, every version of who they were is kept in a form that can be replanted decades later. Not a backup of files, a vault of states. A grandchild could grow the same plan from the same seed.",
  works="Rather than storing results, the system stores the conditions and inputs that produced them, in an append-only record with the reasoning attached. Any past state can be reconstructed exactly, including which engines were involved and what they believed at the time. Later engines can be run against older states to ask what would have been different. Nothing is ever overwritten, so the history cannot quietly change.",
  patentable="Systems keep audit logs of what happened; they do not keep reconstructable states that later inventions can be run against retroactively. The emergent capability is a multi-generational record where future tools can be applied to past lives, which is what makes a family office durable across generations.",
  alice=8, alice_why="Reconstructable-state storage enabling retroactive re-execution is a concrete architecture, clearly beyond ordinary logging.",
  priority="Critical to file",
  urgency="Multi-generational continuity is the promise the whole business rests on, and nothing currently protects it. The retroactive re-execution property is unusual enough that an examiner will see the novelty quickly. It also becomes more valuable every year it runs, which means filing late costs you the earliest and most valuable history. This is the one filing that is genuinely about the next fifty years."),
]
